# beatles 1.29 - port for The Beatles 1.29.0 (Spike 2, plain-C rules on the Godzilla-generation framework).
# Placed at the desk from the card's /beatles/game (sha1 89bdc7b3f2ed1eaf6b8b6213ab1b199fbb56b91d); the two
# words on every `site` line were written by port_words.py --write from the ELF, never typed.
#
# EMULATOR-PROVEN 2026-09-23 (four runs on a copy of beatles-1_29_0.Release.8G, PAD_AUDIO=0):
#   run A  census_mode.c with this port's scoring pair named score_add / scores (census_mode.c never scores):
#          all 26 sites matched, 9 of 9 events armed; 34 of 34 switch rows as the desk map said (24 shots,
#          3 bank completions, 10 controls with no bit); ball end on 2 drains and a tilted ball; 8 of 9 events seen.
#   run B  a call probe (call_probe.c plus a globals watch) on 24 functions, no runtime: score_add32(player r0,
#          u32 points r1) adds points into scores32[player-1] (u32); the watched scores32[0] ended at
#          2,114,750, the number on the glass.
#   run C  template_mode.c + the runtime's 32-bit scoring (score_add32 / scores32) + THIS port: TARGET RUSH started
#          on Left orbit target x3, scored +1,000,000..+9,000,000 per shot, ended on a drain (END (ball ended))
#          and on its clock (END (time ran out)); pm_score read 134,110 then 21,185,510, and the glass showed
#          66,214,710 = 21,185,510 + 45,000,000 + the game's own 29,200.
#   run D  run A's set-up, seven drains: only 3 ended a ball (4 did not: no ball end, no bus 0x34, ball 3 still on the glass);
#          the third ball end was the last ball: game_over 0x47 fired 7.3 s later with bonus_end, in_game 0.
#   runs E-H (2026-09-23, the runtime with switch shots, the bus ball end and the 32-bit headroom cut; PAD_AUDIO=0):
#   run E  census_mode.c + this port: each of switches 73-76 and 48-51 gave exactly one shot (0x100000000 ..
#          0x8000000000) on the tick's thread, none in attract; the slingshots 60/61 gave nothing; the 27 rule shots
#          came as in run A. A mode file (prebuilt mode.so) started on Target 1 and scored Target 2-4 and both
#          return lanes; its total matched the glass (score 7,000 -> 36,023,120).
#   run F  census_mode.c + this port WITHOUT `site ball_end`: the ball end came from bus 0x34 in the dispatch, once
#          per ball on 3 drains (one of them a tilted ball); template_mode.c the same way: END (ball ended).
#   run G  template_mode.c + this port: every award was added in full (+1,000,000..+9,000,000), the glass agreed.
#   run H  godzilla_le-1.16.port and jaws_le-1.02.port on this game: refused on their 4 core sites, stock play.
#   Not exercised: multiball_start (no multiball
#   played), callout_nth / countdown 385 by ear (audio muted), screens, messages, award screens, and lamps as a
#   mode would drive them.
#
# !! SCORING IS 32-BIT HERE: score_add(u8 player r0, u32 points r1) -> u32 (returns points x the byte
#   multiplier 0x543534) and the scores are u32[4]. So the two entries are named `site score_add32` and
#   `data scores32`, the runtime's 32-bit scoring pair (MODE_SDK.md, "Ports"): a runtime from before it finds
#   no core `score_add` / `scores` and hooks NOTHING (fail-closed), instead of passing 64-bit points in r2:r3.
game           beatles
version        1.29

# ---- functions: site <name> <address> <first two instruction words> --------------------
# hooked by the runtime
#   tick: the framework's 60 Hz tick body, the same code as Godzilla Pro 1.15's 0x4ec828 (strict
#   signature from both references; dispatches bus ids 0x37 at entry and 0x38 at exit, called from
#   the process dispatcher loop 0x1ab444, the twin of Godzilla's 0x254ca8). HIGH.
# EMU run A: hooked; tick callbacks on the game thread (thread 547), census ready 9.4 s after the runtime loaded. PROVEN.
site tick             0x000c0210 0xe92d4038 0xe3a00037
#   shot_dispatch: 0x3e314 = the one function every Beatles shot reaches, with the shot's ONE bit in
#   r0 (32 bits). The central shot function 0x419c8(mask) (37 callers, all constant single bits: the
#   switch handler stubs 0x7b8b8..0x7bc9c and the drop-bank handlers) ends every path in
#   `bl 0x3e314` (0x41a0c); the two spinner handlers (0x6be50 / 0x6cc54) call 0x3e314 directly with
#   0x10000000 / 0x20000000 on the first spin of a spin session. Words cmp r0,#0x800 / push: movable.
#   A C framework: no 0x1 pre-dispatch, one bit per call. HIGH (desk); prove with the census.
# EMU run A: one 32-bit bit in r0 per shot; 118 shot callbacks, every one as the desk map below said. PROVEN.
site shot_dispatch    0x0003e314 0xe3500b02 0xe92d4008
#   ball_end: a handler of bus hook 0x34 (the framework's end of ball, dispatched at 0x122ab8 by
#   0x122984, the twin of Godzilla's 0x1f07bc in 0x1f0688). Beatles registers four 0x34 handlers,
#   all priority 0, all returning 1 (none vetoes): 0x35a44 (starts with a bl: not movable),
#   0x3fe54, 0x4b5e8 (subscribed at 0x4d370), 0x336d80 (framework HookListener fan-out). This one is
#   `push; mov r0,#0; bl 0x4b538; mov r0,#1; pop`, reached only through the bus. MEDIUM-HIGH;
#   prove with a drain (END (ball ended)). Alternative: 0x3fe54.
# EMU run A: ran 0.78 s after each drain mark (x2) and on the tilted ball's drain, 16 ms before bus 0x34;
#   run B: called from 0x2e1580 (the bus dispatch loop), r0 = 0; run C: END (ball ended). PROVEN.
#   0x3fe54 (the alternative 0x34 handler) ran at the same three moments (run B).
site ball_end         0x0004b5e8 0xe92d4008 0xe3a00000
#   ball_end_event: the same end of ball as a bus id, for a runtime reading a port with no ball_end site
#   (the runtime hands it to the modes from the dispatch; with the site above it is not used).
# EMU run F (this port without `site ball_end`): one ball end per drain from the dispatch, beside event 0x34. PROVEN.
value ball_end_event       0x34
#   sound_lookup: the framework's key -> entry lookup (strict from Godzilla Pro 1.15 and TMNT 1.58).
#   BOOT-ONLY on Godzilla (memory note); PM_CAN_OWN_SOUND rides on it. HIGH (placement).
# EMU run B: 120+ calls, all during boot (before the Start), none in play - BOOT-ONLY as on Godzilla.
#   Runs A and C hooked it (own-sound armed) with no fault. Placement proven; a mode's own sound not tried.
site sound_lookup     0x002d84a8 0xe92d4038 0xe1a05000
# called
#   score_add: 0x15ee3c(u8 player, u32 points) -> u32. Same framework body as Godzilla's 0x4b8cf4
#   (mode_mask & 0x210 -> error 0x18; player check 0x159a80 -> error 0x19; points *= the byte
#   multiplier at 0x543534; bus 0xa1 veto / 0xa2; scores[p-1] += points; notifiers; bus 0xa5) but
#   32-BIT: `ldr r3,[r5,r2,lsl#2]; add; str`. Callers pass (ldrb player, u32 points) at 0x122d3c
#   and 0x18aa1c; 0x15ef84 = score_add(current player, r0) with 26 callers. HIGH for the site;
#   named score_add32 for its calling convention (see the header).
# EMU run B: r0 = 1 (player), r1 = points (5000, 1000, 100...); scores32[0] rose by exactly r1 x mult (mult 1)
#   after each call; 0x15ef84 = score_add(current player, r0) called it every time. Run C: +45,000,000 on the
#   glass through the runtime's 32-bit scoring. PROVEN (32-bit convention).
site score_add32      0x0015ee3c 0xe30435de 0xe3a02000
#   callout / callout_nth: the framework sound requests (Jaws's port uses them the same way; port_tool
#   from Jaws: through the handler of hook 0xa6; from Godzilla: through the handler of hook 0x95).
#   Beatles calls 0x23f87c(request) 264 times and 0x23fa30(request, n) for its countdown. HIGH.
# EMU run B: 120 calls (cap), 116 after the Start, r0 = request ids (0x102 on a target, 0x169, 0x177, 0x132...).
#   Called by the game as a request(id) function: placement PROVEN; a mode's call not heard (muted).
site callout          0x0023f87c 0xe92d4010 0xe30be698
# EMU run B: 0 calls (the challenge mode's countdown was not played). Run C: the runtime called it with
#   countdown 385 for seconds 5..1 with no fault. Id not verified by ear.
site callout_nth      0x0023fa30 0xe92d4010 0xe30be698
#   lamp_group: the lamp-group wrapper, instruction for instruction Godzilla Pro 1.15's 0x4bf294; it
#   calls the allocator 0x2e10c8, whose 60 words equal Godzilla's allocator 0x3c14d4 (masked). HIGH.
# EMU run B: 120 calls (11 in attract, 109 in play). Called; not driven by a mode.
site lamp_group       0x000a269c 0xe92d4038 0xe1a04000
#   show_priority: located (strict) from Godzilla and TMNT. Used only by pm_lights (off: no light_run).
# EMU run B: 120 calls alongside lamp_group. Called; pm_lights stays off (no light_run).
site show_priority    0x0011e8e8 0xe3053d04 0xe340305b
#   award_screen: located (strict). The game itself calls it as 0x135978(type, 0, 0, 0x53f474) and
#   writes the message id at +0xa0 and the value at +0xa8 (the skill shot, 0x593a4..0x593b8). HIGH.
# EMU run B: 120 calls, every one with r3 = 0x53f474 (award_screen_arg), r0 = effect ids (0x0d, 0x37, 0x1d,
#   0x64 on every target, 0x77, 0x78...). A general display-effect start, as on Godzilla. Not driven by a mode.
site award_screen     0x00135978 0xe92d4070 0xe24dd008
#   string_new / dynamic_cast: PLT stubs (_ZNSsC1EPKcRKSaIcE, __dynamic_cast); weak check by design.
site string_new       0x000167e0 0xe28fc605 0xe28cca27
site dynamic_cast     0x000161e0 0xe28fc605 0xe28cca27
#   resource_get: placed through 3 callers (port_tool, from Godzilla and from TMNT). MEDIUM.
# EMU run B: 76 calls (22 at boot). Called.
site resource_get     0x003c6964 0xe92d43f0 0xe1a04000
#   find_node / find_text: Radium's find<Sprite> / find<Text> template instantiations. Beatles has the
#   same 10 instantiations as Godzilla in the same order (two groups of Text/Spine/Sound/Sprite/Video,
#   told apart by the typeinfo each casts to through its GOT slot, findnode.py); the port's are the
#   second group (generic finder 0x42c734 here, 0x577a4c on Godzilla; both groups 0x1e88 apart on
#   both builds). HIGH (desk).
# EMU run B: 120 calls at boot. Called; arguments not decoded.
site find_node        0x0042d714 0xe92d4070 0xe24dd008
# EMU run B: 120 calls (98 in play). Called; arguments not decoded.
site find_text        0x0042d1b0 0xe92d4070 0xe24dd008
#   set_text: located (strict).
# EMU run B: 120 calls at boot. Called.
site set_text         0x00410edc 0xe92d47f0 0xe1a06000
#   surface_state / player_advance / display_draw: located (strict). Clips stay OFF: Beatles has no
#   clip_play / clip_stop / video_player / video_surface (see the comment block after the data lines).
# EMU run B: surface_state, player_advance, display_draw 120 calls each at boot. Called.
site surface_state    0x00420440 0xe5900550 0xe2800008
site player_advance   0x00135d70 0xe2501000 0x012fff1e
site display_draw     0x001e2e04 0xe3520001 0x812fff1e

# ---- globals: data <name> <address> ---------------------------------------------------------
#   cur_player: the byte current_player() 0x159b90 reads (the twin of Godzilla's 0x460ba0; 520
#   callers). port_tool: derived from 2 places. HIGH.
# EMU run B: the byte reads 1 from boot (attract too) and through the game; run A: player 1 on all 118 shots. PROVEN.
data cur_player             0x0054322c
#   scores: u32[4] (NOT u64): score_add adds into [0x5b3578 + 4*(p-1)]; the getters 0x15edb8 /
#   0x15edd4 read `ldr r0,[r3,r0,lsl#2]`; 0x15f090 zeroes four words. HIGH; named scores32.
# EMU run B: u32[4]; [0] = 2,114,750 at the end = the glass. Run C: pm_score read it. PROVEN.
data scores32               0x005b3578
#   score_mult: the playfield multiplier byte score_add32 multiplies the points by before it adds them
#   (0x15ee7c movw/movt 0x543534; ldrb r3,[r3]; mul r1, r3, r5). The runtime cuts an award to the room left
#   below 4,294,967,295 divided by it, so an award never wraps the u32 score. Read only. Desk (run B saw mult 1).
# EMU runs E-G: named on the boot line; every award below the room was added in full. The cut itself not reached.
data score_mult             0x00543534
#   mode_mask: the u16 the switch drain (0x1f8ad8) and score_add (0x15ee48, tst #0x210) read. HIGH.
# EMU run B: 0x10 in attract, 0x20 for 4 ms at the Start, 0 in play, 0x4 then 0x5 at end of ball/bonus,
#   0x200 on tilt, 0x204 at the tilted ball's end. So busy 0x210 = attract | tilt: run A logged in_game 0 on
#   the tilt and 1 everywhere else in play. PROVEN.
data mode_mask              0x005b45de
#   event_head / event_current: the process list; the switch handlers read [[0x5b5d04]+0xa0] = the
#   switch number of the process running. derived from 2 places. HIGH.
data event_head             0x005b5d00
data event_current          0x005b5d04
#   resource_manager / display_holder: derived from 2 places.
data resource_manager       0x005b18b0
data display_holder         0x005b1830
#   typeinfo_resource / typeinfo_scene_player: derived from 2 places (from Jaws), and the Beatles game
#   code itself casts the video bank's resource with exactly these two (0x3e874..0x3e888). HIGH.
data typeinfo_resource      0x004b4528
data typeinfo_scene_player  0x004c294c
#   message_count / message_remap / message_table: derived from 2 places.
data message_count          0x0049bdcc
data message_remap          0x005b70a0
data message_table          0x0055a500
#   award_screen_arg: derived from 2 places, and the game passes it as r3 to award_screen. HIGH.
data award_screen_arg       0x0053f474
# NOT PLACED - clips: Godzilla's and Jaws's clip_play(name,0,0) / video_surface() / video_player()
#   are THEIR game library's helpers (Godzilla 0x528a4, low text), not the framework's. Beatles has
#   no such function: 13 Beatles game functions each find the video bank 60ed7e50 and its
#   "VideoSurface" node inline (e.g. 0x3e828, a "clip with a total" helper, 12 callers), through
#   0x137094 (resource by name), find<Video> 0x42da08 and 0x4250ec (play by name). pm_clip needs a
#   runtime path composed from those primitives (not written yet).
# NOT PLACED - light_run (pm_lights): no framework function of that shape (absent from every reference
#   draft); lamps below do not need it.

# ---- offsets, flags and ids: value <name> <number> -----------------------------------------
# the shot dispatch carries ONE 32-bit bit in r0 (the runtime reads r[shot_mask_at])
value shot_mask_at          0
# EMU run A: 32 bits in r0 (shot_mask_at 0). PROVEN.
value shot_mask_bits        32
# busy = 0x210: score_add itself refuses while mode_mask & 0x210 (0x15ee50). HIGH.
value mode_mask_busy        0x210
# framework offsets COPIED (the same framework code; the scene's +0x18 mutex and +0x10 scene are read
# the same way by the Beatles game code 0x3e8a8 / 0x3e8d4). scene_player_scene HIGH, the rest copied.
value scene_player_scene    0x10
value node_visible_vfn      0xa8
value display_at            0x7c
value surface_playing       2
value clip_layer            0
# the award node's fields, as the game writes them (+0xa0 message, +0xa8 value) at 0x593b0/0x593b8;
# +0xb0 copied
value award_message_at      0xa0
value award_value_at        0xa8
value award_count_at        0xb0
# award_screen_type is a title's effect id. CANDIDATE, not proven: 0x3a (58), the effect the skill
#   shot award asks for with a message and a value (0x593a0); 0x43 (67) the left bank's (0x33f84).
# value award_screen_type     58
# event_* offsets are only for pm_lights, which is off (no light_run); left out.

# ---- shots: shot <mask> <name> -------------------------------------------------------------------
# DESK map from the handlers: every switch handler stub passes a constant
# bit to 0x419c8. NOT a census: prove each with census_mode.c (switch ids for swpoke in the comments).
# Drop targets fire their bit when the bank's handler sees the target go down (0x2ef40 / 0x2f19c,
# 0x2fae8 / 0x2fd70, 0x1f604 / 0x1f88c, jump tables keyed on the switch id).
shot 0x2           FAB drop F
shot 0x4           FAB drop A
shot 0x8           FAB drop B
shot 0x10          FAB bank completed
shot 0x20          FOUR drop F
shot 0x40          FOUR drop O
shot 0x80          FOUR drop U
shot 0x100         FOUR drop R
shot 0x200         FOUR bank completed
shot 0x400         1964 drop 1
shot 0x800         1964 drop 9
shot 0x1000        1964 drop 6
shot 0x2000        1964 drop 4
shot 0x4000        1964 bank completed
shot 0x8000        Left pop bumper
shot 0x10000       Top pop bumper
shot 0x20000       Right pop bumper
shot 0x400000      Left orbit target
shot 0x800000      Right orbit target
shot 0x1000000     Lower left target
shot 0x2000000     Super jackpot target
shot 0x4000000     Left orbit
shot 0x8000000     Right orbit
shot 0x10000000    Left spinner
shot 0x20000000    Right spinner
shot 0x40000000    Skill shot rollover
shot 0x80000000    Top orbit
# switch -> bit (desk): 52 LT 3 BANK DROP LT 0x2, 53 CNTR 0x4, 54 RT 0x8; 85 CNTR 4 BANK DROP LT 0x20,
# 86 LT CNTR 0x40, 87 R-CNTR 0x80, 88 RT 0x100; 78 RT 4 BANK DROP LEFT 0x400, 79 LT CTR 0x800,
# 80 R-CNTR 0x1000, 81 RIGHT 0x2000; 89 LEFT POP 0x8000, 91 TOP POP 0x10000, 90 RIGHT POP 0x20000 (the
# pops by audit name: 0x7b8b8 LEFT BUMPER, 0x7b8f0 CENTER BUMPER, 0x7b8d4 RIGHT BUMPER);
# 77 LEFT ORBIT TARGET 0x400000, 84 RIGHT ORBIT TARGET 0x800000, 43 LOWER LEFT TARGET 0x1000000,
# 44 SUPER JACKPOT TARGET 0x2000000, 70 LEFT ORBIT OPTO 0x4000000 (conditional on the orbit
# timers 0x17/0x18), 72 RIGHT ORBIT OPTO 0x8000000 (conditional), 92 SPINNER LEFT 0x10000000,
# 82 SPINNER RIGHT ORBIT 0x20000000, 83 SKILL SHOT ROLLOVER 0x40000000, 71 TOP MAGNET OPTO
# 0x80000000 (conditional on timer 0x1d). No bit: TARGET 1-4 (73-76, the JOHN/PAUL/GEORGE/RINGO
# standups, 0x5a8f8), the lanes (48-51), the slings (60, 61). Unused bits: 0x1, 0x40000-0x200000.

# ---- shots from switches: switch <id> <shot mask> <name> (MODE_SDK.md, "Shots from switches") -----------
# The rules send no bit for the four standups or the lanes, but the framework's switch drain (0x1f8a78, Godzilla's
# 0x1e7540 word for word) broadcasts every switch whose descriptor flags ask for it, once per hit, on the same edge
# the switch's own handler runs on: flag 0x2000 through 0x96e68(switch id) (bus 0xcf), flag 0x1000 through
# 0x96f08(switch id) (bus 0xce). Descriptors ([0x544624] = 0x570284, 0x28 bytes each, flags at +0x1a): 73-76 are
# 0x1400 (0x96f08), 48-51 are 0x2400 (0x96e68). Only in play: the drain skips a switch while mode_mask shares no
# bit with its flags (attract 0x10, bonus 0x5). 0x96e68 is called only by the drain (0x1f8bd4) and 0x1f8a6c;
# 0x96f08 also by the drop banks (0x1f638, 0x2ef74, 0x2fb1c) for their own switches, which no line maps.
# The slingshots (60, 61) have no flag: nothing broadcasts them, so they cannot be mapped here.
# Words subs/bxeq and push/subs: movable; no branch lands on +4 of either.
# EMU run E: both hooked; 73-76 and 48-51 each gave exactly one shot in play, none in attract; 60/61 nothing. PROVEN.
site switch_hit       0x00096e68 0xe2503000 0x012fff1e
site switch_hit2      0x00096f08 0xe92d4010 0xe2504000
switch 73          0x100000000     Target 1
switch 74          0x200000000     Target 2
switch 75          0x400000000     Target 3
switch 76          0x800000000     Target 4
switch 48          0x1000000000    Left outlane
switch 49          0x2000000000    Left return lane
switch 50          0x4000000000    Right return lane
switch 51          0x8000000000    Right outlane

# ---- callouts by role, scenes by role -------------------------------------------------------------
# countdown: the challenge mode's song clock (0x40f70, AD_CHALLENGE_MODE_SONG_SECONDS) plays
# sound_nth(385, seconds left - 1) for its last 10 s (0x41030..0x41038). Desk; not heard.
callout countdown           385
# ten_seconds / time_up: NOT FOUND (no Beatles timed mode plays a separate request at 10 s or 0 s that
#   this read found); left out, so the Modes tab greys "Sound: count down" and the game's own call.
# video_bank: the same id as Godzilla's; 13 Beatles functions load it and find "VideoSurface" in it.
scene video_bank           60ed7e5036b8ce09d35a3e101ea6fc1380b37d97
# hud / attract: NOT PLACED. Beatles names only 7 top-level scenes in code (937b6a26 bonus tally,
#   60ed7e50 bank, ffa461e7, 05d1c47b, d1e3403b, 08065a0c Element_4x3, 713deecc); none is the score
#   panel or Godzilla's slide-out HUD. A screen needs a measured HUD scene (scene_write profile).

