# city_variants: Godzilla's RuleCities map; Beatles has none (left out).

# ---- the game's own modes: NO cmode_manager, so no stock_* sites (pm_stock_mode_running -> -1).
# Witness CANDIDATE for a runtime that can read data witnesses (not written yet): the main
# multiball rule's per-player state u32 [0x582d28 + 4*(player-1)]: 3 while a multiball runs (written by
# the multiball start 0x39270 at 0x392ac), 0 at every end of ball (0x35a7c). Not read live.

# ---- events: the same framework bus as Godzilla (subscribe 0x2e149c, dispatch 0x2e1548, table
# 0x5bc828, ids 0..207; both functions instruction for instruction Godzilla's 0x4bb380 / 0x4bb42c).
# EMU run A: hooked; the runtime's dispatch counter ran on thread 1 and delivered the ids below. PROVEN.
site hook_dispatch    0x002e1548 0xe35000cf 0xe92d4038
# The ids below are dispatched by the framework's game-flow functions at the SAME code places as on
# Godzilla Pro 1.15, where each was measured: ball start 0x1223b8 (GZ 0x1f00bc), game start 0x1225b0
# (0x1f02b4), game over 0x122884 (0x1f0588), end of ball 0x122ab8 (0x1f07bc), bonus 0x122c5c /
# 0x122c70 (0x1f0960 / 0x1f0974), tilt 0x177f0c (0x4b349c), tilt warning 0x177ff8 (0x4b3588).
# DESK placement; all 8 bus ids were measured on Beatles in runs A and D (see the EMU lines above game_start).
# EMU run A (one marked game): game_start 0x4d and ball_start 0x25 at the Start; ball_end 0x34 at each drain and the
#   tilted ball; bonus_start 0x27 0.7 s after a drain's end and 1.2 s after the last; bonus_end 0x28 with the next
#   ball_start ~9 s later; tilt_warning 0xc8 on pendulum hits 1 and 2; tilt 0xc6 on hit 3; no bonus after the tilt.
#   Run D: game_over 0x47 once, 7.3 s after the last ball's end (with bonus_end, in_game 0), and never before it;
#   4 drains that did not end a ball sent no ball_end. All 8 bus ids are PROVEN; the site event multiball_start is not.
event game_start      0x4d
event ball_start      0x25
event ball_end        0x34
event bonus_start     0x27
event bonus_end       0x28
event tilt_warning    0xc8
event tilt            0xc6
event game_over       0x47
#   mball_start: the multiball intro process body 0x3559c, posted ONLY by the multiball start 0x39270
#   (event_post(0xa1, 0x3559c, 2) at 0x39450) after its "MAIN/TAXMAN MULTIBALL STARTED" audits, for
#   both multiballs (its +0xa0 is the taxman flag). Words movw/mov: movable. MEDIUM (desk).
# EMU run B: 0 calls - no multiball was played. NOT TESTED.
site mball_start      0x0003559c 0xe3051d04 0xe3a02000
event multiball_start site mball_start
# skill_shot: NOT PLACED. The award is inline in 0x592c8, which every skill-rollover / top-orbit /
#   top-pop shot calls (its audits 0x93/0x94/0x95 sit inside); no function runs only on an award.

# ---- display priority: display_effect_start 0x2e0420, display_effect_next 0x2e0804,
# display_priority_now 0x2e0c98 (strict) and display_effects 0x5bc510 (one place) exist, but the layered
# display half (layered_priority, layered_waiter, layered_displays) is Godzilla's game library and has
# no Beatles counterpart, so the lines are
# left out. The runtime can arm the effect half alone (MODE_SDK.md, "Display priority"), but Beatles'
# display_host (the effect a game runs under the others) is not measured, so no display line is here yet.

# ---- named inserts: framework lamp layers (the allocator 0x2e10c8 is Godzilla's 0x3c14d4 word for word)
#   lamp_layers: derived from 2 places (0x3c14d4+0x8 on Godzilla); light_count: derived from 2 places.
data lamp_layers            0x005bc520
data light_count            0x005931f0
value lamp_slot_size        40
value lamp_slot_level       2
value lamp_slot_alpha       3
value lamp_slot_fade        8
value lamp_slot_used        36
value lamp_group_prio       4
value lamp_group_next       20
# lamp_fade: Godzilla's in-play value, COPIED (not read on Beatles)
value lamp_fade             3
